@title EPISODE 01 • FIRST IMPRESSIONS
@bg track_stadium_morning
Six a.m. Maple Valley University. The track is still wet, the sky is pink, and London Sterling is already annoyed.
@show london
Holloway: Sterling. You're late.
London: I'm four minutes early to the part of practice that matters.
Holloway: Cute. Two extra laps. Want to try for three?
> [Bitchy] "Put it on my dad's tab." -> c1_bitchy
> [Sweet] "Sorry, Coach. Won't happen again." -> c1_sweet
> [Bold] Start running before she finishes. -> c1_bold
> [Bad] "Traffic was crazy." (It wasn't.) -> c1_bad
*c1_bitchy
@add Coach_Respect -2
@add London_Confidence 1
Holloway: Your dad's tab doesn't cover my patience. Three laps.
London: Worth it.
@jump c1_done
*c1_sweet
@add Coach_Respect 2
Holloway: ...Huh. Okay. Two laps, and I'm writing down the date.
@jump c1_done
*c1_bold
@add Coach_Respect 1
@add London_Confidence 1
Holloway: (calling after her) That still counts as talking back, Sterling!
@jump c1_done
*c1_bad
@add Coach_Respect -1
Holloway: You live eleven minutes away in a penthouse with a driver. Three laps.
*c1_done
@show diggy
Halfway through lap two, a sprinter jogs past going the wrong direction. Grey hoodie. Annoying smile.
Diggy: Daddy's donation don't cover cardio, huh?
> [Bitchy] "Did I ask you something?" -> c2_bitchy
> [Bold] "Worry about your 400, sprinter." -> c2_bold
> [Sweet] Laugh. "Okay, that was a little funny." -> c2_sweet
> [Good] Ignore him and keep your pace. -> c2_good
*c2_bitchy
@add Diggy_Trust -1
Diggy: Nah. But you answered anyway.
London: Keep running into people, you'll be a 400 guy with a 600 time.
Diggy: Ooh. You know my event. I'm flattered.
@jump c2_done
*c2_bold
@add Diggy_Affection 2
Diggy: Oh, she knows my event.
London: I know everybody's event. It's called paying attention. Try it.
@jump c2_done
*c2_sweet
@add Diggy_Affection 1
@add Diggy_Trust 1
Diggy: See? She human.
London: Barely. Don't tell anyone.
@jump c2_done
*c2_good
@add London_Confidence 1
London runs past him without a glance. He laughs anyway. Somehow that's worse.
*c2_done
@bg locker_room
@show paris
Paris: Can you please not start a war on day one?
London: He started it.
Paris: You started it in your head three weeks ago when you saw his name on the roster.
London: I don't even know his name.
Paris: Duncan Williams. Everybody calls him Diggy. You said it twice in the car.
> [Bitchy] "Mind your business, Paris." -> c3_bitchy
> [Sweet] "...Okay, maybe I said it once." -> c3_sweet
> [Bold] "Because he's annoying. Twice." -> c3_bold
*c3_bitchy
@add Paris_Friendship -2
Paris goes quiet and ties her spikes a little too tight. London feels it, and doesn't apologize. Yet.
@jump c3_done
*c3_sweet
@add Paris_Friendship 2
Paris: Mm-hm. I'm telling Mom.
London: You will not.
@jump c3_done
*c3_bold
@add Paris_Friendship 1
Paris: Annoying people don't usually get their name said twice.
*c3_done
@show cassie
Cassie: (sliding in) Okay, who's annoying? Because I have a list and I'm accepting additions.
London: Nobody.
Cassie: Nobody is a sprinter, six-one, curly hair, waits tables at my mom's restaurant on Thursdays and Saturdays?
Paris covers her mouth. London stares at the ceiling and asks God for patience.
